Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.65,0:00:02.78,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,What if money actually grew on trees?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.65,0:00:09.57,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,At first, everyone would think
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.79,0:00:11.22,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,they had just become rich.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.65,0:00:17.29,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,Then every tree on Earth
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.51,0:00:19.36,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,starts producing cash.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.65,0:00:26.28,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,Suddenly, almost everyone has more money
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.50,0:00:27.98,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,than they can spend.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.65,0:00:33.12,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,But there is one problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.34,0:00:35.45,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,More money does not mean more food,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.67,0:00:37.53,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,houses, or resources.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.65,0:00:41.56,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,As cash becomes unlimited,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.78,0:00:44.15,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,prices could rise faster and faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.65,0:00:50.17,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,Eventually, those piles of money
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.39,0:00:52.18,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,might barely buy anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.65,0:00:57.96,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,Because real wealth is not just money.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.18,0:01:00.63,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,It is the things people can actually produce.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.65,0:01:06.55,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,The richest person in this world
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.77,0:01:08.98,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,might still be unable to buy dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.65,0:01:14.80,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,Would you still want money to grow on trees?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.02,0:01:16.51,Subtitle,,0,0,0,,Tell us: yes or no?
